<!DOCTYPE RCC><RCC version="1.0">
    <!-- Runtime path :/names/player_names.json - the alias strips the source
         directory, as table.qrc does.

         THE NAMES NEW GAME GIVES THE BOTS, drawn at random (src/ui/PlayerNames.h).
         One entry per name, in any order:
         - "name": as it is shown, at most 20 characters (the panels' limit).
         - "gender": "male", "female", or "any" for a name either can have.
         - "language": "ro" or "en", the app's language it is drawn in, or "any"
           for both.
         - "strategy" (optional): the bot strategy it is dedicated to. Only a bot
           of that strategy is given it, and that bot is given its strategy's
           names of its gender whenever there are any free. The names: random,
           first-card, low-risk, ducking, cyborg, reckoner-alpha, reckoner-beta,
           reckoner-gamma, reckoner-delta (newgame::avatarStrategyOf()).
         For example:
           { "name": "T-800", "gender": "male", "language": "any",
             "strategy": "cyborg" }
         PlayerNamesTests fails on an entry the app would skip, and on a strategy
         the game does not have. -->
    <qresource prefix="/names">
        <file alias="player_names.json">names/player_names.json</file>
    </qresource>
</RCC>
